[[0,1361726,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-22T02:02:07","1361726","[A]",[],"<p><a href=\"https://voat.co/user/arrgg/submissions\">https://voat.co/user/arrgg/submissions</a></p>\n<p>Occasional posts over the past year, mostly negative against RNC / GOP, Trump, and / or Russia. But, since yesterday, lots of activity from this guy. Same trend, but now most of his links are labelled as the opposite of what they link to in order to farm upvotes from people who don't click the actual link. Like, the article is clearly anti-Trump, but he puts the opposite of the title of the article. Same MSM bs we are used to, but now with clickbait headlines. Also seems to be avoiding <a href=\"https://voat.co/v/news\">v/news</a> as well while he hadn't been before, probably because misleading titles aren't allowed there.</p>","Shenanigans Detected: @arrgg","","ReportCTR"]]
